  "comment": "Pose guides for the 4-direction walk sheet; same conventions as turnaround.json. Four frames per row in the standard order contact, passing, contact, passing -- frames 0 and 2 plant both feet with opposite legs leading, frames 1 and 3 lift the swinging leg and raise the body by 0.02 of a cell. Arms swing against the legs. The front and back rows use a much smaller stride than the profile rows on purpose: a stride drawn towards the camera reads as a stumble, so those rows carry the cycle in the body bob and the lifted foot instead.",
